hillsdale college is unique in so many  ways and by my father's great vision and  luck I had the privilege of going there  at Hillsdale we believe strongly that  students have to come to college to  learn and they have to learn a number of  different things and they also have to  learn what they want to do if they don't  already know and sometimes what they  think they want to do changes as they go  along that path in college ninety-six  percent of our graduates six months are  either gainfully employed or they're  attending graduate school and continuing  their education in some way shape or  form we're very proud of those numbers  and the TDC companies and cleaves has  been very helpful in having us achieve  that number and achieve that goal in a  number of different ways first and  foremost they come to campus and they  talk to our students they interview our  students they give us opportunities to  have our students go to DDC companies  and do some job shadowing we have a  number of students that have internships  in the summertime and the real  internships a lot of times students will  get internships with bigger companies  and they'll be making copies or they  might be getting the coffee we know from  the feedback we get and the assessments  we get after interns come back from TDC  companies that we're doing real work  they're part of a real team they're  making real contributions they're  looking at the needs of whatever client  they might be working with that TDC is  helping and they're adding value to that  team and the service that TDC is  providing that client and that's  something that's just invaluable for our  students because it helps them  understand what they're going to do  after they graduate and it helps them  make a better decision and hopefully  maybe in some cases lead to full-time  employment did Hillsdale College teach  me stuff that becomes important in what  I do day-to-day over the last 25 years  i'd say directly no but more importantly  they gave me a greater gift they taught  me how to learn so that's why i love  Hillsdale College
 

